Stage 2 — LiDAR-to-Camera Projection

Task 1: Verify Projection Setup

Objective: Verify the camera image, LiDAR point cloud, and calibration parameters before projecting LiDAR points onto the image.

Implementation:

Loaded camera image and Velodyne LiDAR data for frame 0000000100.

Read the camera-to-Velodyne transformation matrix and inverted it to transform LiDAR points into camera coordinates.

Applied camera rectification and the projection matrix from perspective.txt.

Calculated projected pixel coordinates and filtered points outside the image boundaries.

Results:

Image resolution: 1408 × 376

Valid LiDAR points: 109,355

Points in front of the camera: 56,300

Points inside image bounds: 26,599

Outcome: Confirmed that the projection pipeline produces valid image coordinates. Calibration direction and coordinate conventions still require verification.

Task 2: Project LiDAR Points onto the Camera Image

Objective: Visualize the projected LiDAR points over the camera image to inspect spatial alignment.

Implementation:

Transformed LiDAR points into camera coordinates.

Applied rectification and the camera projection matrix.

Filtered points that were behind the camera or outside image boundaries.

Overlaid the projected points on the camera image.

Used depth-based colors to distinguish near and far points.

Output:

results/0000000100_lidar_overlay.png

Results:

Frame: 0000000100

Valid projected points: 26,599

Visualized the LiDAR distribution across the road, vehicles, and surrounding scene.

Outcome: Generated a LiDAR–camera overlay for visual inspection. The alignment appears plausible, but exact calibration accuracy has not yet been established.

